text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', "Aeronaut Tinkerer has flying as long as you control an artifact. (It can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", "Artifact spells you cast have convoke. (Your creatures can help cast those spells. Each creature you tap while casting an artifact spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)", "As Phyrexian Revoker enters the battlefield, choose a nonland card name.\\nActivated abilities of sources with the chosen name can't be activated.", "As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nDraw cards equal to the sacrificed creature's power.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice an artifact.\\nShrapnel Blast deals 5 damage to any target.', "As long as you control an artifact, Scrapyard Mongrel gets +2/+0 and has trample. (It can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", 'At the beginning of combat on your turn, if you control each creature on the battlefield with the greatest power, gain control of target creature an opponent controls until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if an opponent lost life last turn, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if you lost life last turn, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token.', "At the beginning of your end step, if you didn't activate a loyalty ability of a planeswalker this turn, you lose 2 life.\\n{4}, {T}: For each planeswalker you control, you may activate one of its loyalty abilities once this turn as though none of its loyalty abilities have been activated this turn.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, create a colorless artifact token named Land Mine with "{R}, Sacrifice this artifact: This artifact deals 2 damage to target attacking creature without flying." Then flip a coin. If you lose the flip, Goblin Kaboomist deals 2 damage to itself.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, return a creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'Blastfire Bolt deals 5 damage to target creature. Destroy all Equipment attached to that creature.', "Cast this spell only if you've cast another spell this turn.\\nFlying", "Charging Rhino can't be blocked by more than one creature.", 'Cone of Flame deals 1 damage to any target, 2 damage to another target, and 3 damage to a third target.', "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nAs Obelisk of Urd enters the battlefield, choose a creature type.\\nCreatures you control of the chosen type get +2/+2.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nChoose a nonland card name. Search target player's graveyard, hand, and library for any number of cards with that name and exile them. Then that player shuffles.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nCovenant of Blood deals 4 damage to any target and you gain 4 life.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nCreate three 1/1 white Spirit creature tokens with flying. (They can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nCreate three 3/3 green Beast creature tokens.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nCreatures you control get +3/+3 until end of turn.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nExile target attacking or blocking creature.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nFlying\\nSeraph of the Masses's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creatures you control.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nPut target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nReturn X target creature cards with mana value 2 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nReturn up to two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nSearch your library for a creature card with mana value X or less, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nSearch your library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nStoke the Flames deals 4 damage to any target.", 'Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature\'s color.)\\nTarget creature gains indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it.)', "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nTarget creature gets +1/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn. (It deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nTarget creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nTrample", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nWhen Living Totem enters the battlefield, you may put a +1/+1 counter on another target creature.", "Convoke (Your creatures can help cast this spell. Each creature you tap while casting this spell pays for {1} or one mana of that creature's color.)\\nYou gain 8 life.", 'Counter target noncreature spell.', 'Counter target spell.', "Counter target spell. If that spell is countered this way, exile it instead of putting it into its owner's graveyard.", 'Counter target spell. If you control a blue creature, draw a card, then discard a card.', 'Create two 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.', 'Creatures you control get +2/+1 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +2/+1 until end of turn. White creatures you control also gain first strike until end of turn. (They deal combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', 'Dauntless River Marshal gets +1/+1 as long as you control an Island.\\n{3}{U}: Tap target creature.', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', 'Deathtouch\\n{3}{B}{B}: Return up to three target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.\\n{3}{B}{B}, Exile Soul of Innistrad from your graveyard: Return up to three target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWhen Coral Barrier enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 blue Squid creature token with islandwalk. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWhenever Hornet Nest is dealt damage, create that many 1/1 green Insect creature tokens with flying and deathtouch. (Any amount of damage a creature with deathtouch deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWhenever Wall of Essence is dealt combat damage, you gain that much life.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWhenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on Wall of Limbs.\\n{5}{B}{B}, Sacrifice Wall of Limbs: Target player loses X life, where X is Wall of Limbs's power.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{3}: Until end of turn, Gargoyle Sentinel loses defender and gains flying.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{G}, Sacrifice a Wall: Draw a card.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{R}: Wall of Fire gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", "Defender\\nWhenever Wall of Frost blocks a creature, that creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", "Destroy all creatures you don't control and all planeswalkers you don't control.", 'Destroy all enchantments.', 'Destroy all nonwhite creatures.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment. You gain 4 life.', 'Destroy target attacking or blocking creature.', 'Destroy target creature with defender.', 'Destroy target creature with flying.', "Destroy target creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Dragon creatures you control get +3/+3.', 'Draw three cards.', 'Draw two cards.', 'Each land is a Swamp in addition to its other land types.', "Enchant artifact or creature\\nEnchanted permanent doesn't untap during its controller's untap step and its activated abilities can't be activated.", 'Enchant artifact\\nEnchanted artifact is a creature with base power and toughness 5/5 in addition to its other types.', 'Enchant creature you control\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+0.\\n{R}, Sacrifice Inferno Fist: Inferno Fist deals 2 damage to any target.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block unless its controller pays {3}.\\nActivated abilities of enchanted creature cost {3} more to activate.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't be blocked except by Walls.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.\\n{4}{G}: Return Vineweft from your graveyard to your hand.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has protection from all colors. This effect doesn't remove Auras. (It can't be blocked, targeted, or dealt damage by anything that's white, blue, black, red, or green.)", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has vigilance. (Attacking doesn't cause it to tap.)", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -1/-1 and can't block.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -2/-2.\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature's controller, that player loses 2 life.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has "{T}: This creature deals damage equal to its power to any target."', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has double strike. (It deals both first-strike and regular combat damage.)', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has lifelink and "Whenever a creature an opponent controls dies, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature." (Damage dealt by a creature with lifelink also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', 'Enchant creature\\nWhen Divine Favor enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+3.', "Enchant creature\\nWhen Hammerhand enters the battlefield, target creature can't block this turn.\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 and has haste.", 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Target player loses 3 life."', 'Enchant land\\nWhen Verdant Haven enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.\\nWhenever enchanted land is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional one mana of any color.', "Equipped creature can't be blocked.\\nWhenever equipped creature is dealt damage, destroy it.\\nEquip {3} ({3}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", 'Equipped creature gets +2/+0 and has vigilance and "At the beginning of your upkeep, draw a card."\\nWhenever equipped creature dies, target opponent gains control of Avarice Amulet.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "Equipped creature gets +2/+2 and has trample. (It can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nEquip {4} ({4}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", "Equipped creature gets +4/+4.\\n{0}: Until end of turn, Haunted Plate Mail becomes a 4/4 Spirit artifact creature that's no longer an Equipment. Activate only if you control no creatures.\\nEquip {4} ({4}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", 'Exile target creature with toughness 4 or greater.', 'Exile the top three cards of your library. Until end of turn, you may play cards exiled this way. (If you cast a spell this way, you still pay its costs. You can play a land this way only if you have an available land play remaining.)', 'First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\nWhenever Preeminent Captain attacks, you may put a Soldier creature card from your hand onto the battlefield tapped and attacking.', "First strike\\n{3}{R}{R}: Soul of Shandalar deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker and 3 damage to up to one target creature that player or that planeswalker's controller controls.\\n{3}{R}{R}, Exile Soul of Shandalar from your graveyard: Soul of Shandalar deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker and 3 damage to up to one target creature that player or that planeswalker's controller controls.", "Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nFlying\\nWhen Quickling enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you return another creature you control to its owner's hand.", "Flash\\nFlying\\nCreatures entering the battlefield don't cause abilities to trigger.", 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nCarrion Crow enters the battlefield tapped.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nFirst strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nLifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nNightmare's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Swamps you control.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWelkin Tern can block only creatures with flying.", 'Flying (This creature can\'t be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhen Aegis Angel enters the battlefield, another target permanent gains indestructible for as long as you control Aegis Angel. (Effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it. A creature with indestructible can\'t be destroyed by damage.)', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Sengir Vampire this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Sengir Vampire.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{R}: Shivan Dragon gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", 'Flying, deathtouch\\nWhen Hornet Queen enters the battlefield, create four 1/1 green Insect creature tokens with flying and deathtouch.', 'Flying, trample\\nWhenever an opponent searches their library, that player sacrifices a creature and loses 10 life.\\nWhenever another creature dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Ob Nixilis, Unshackled.', 'Flying, vigilance', 'Flying, vigilance\\n{1}{W}: Prevent all damage that would be dealt to another target creature this turn by sources of the color of your choice.\\n{5}{W}{W}: Prevent all damage that would be dealt to target player or planeswalker this turn by sources of the color of your choice.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, draw a card unless target opponent sacrifices a creature or pays 3 life.', "Flying\\nWhen Hoarding Dragon enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an artifact card, exile it, then shuffle.\\nWhen Hoarding Dragon dies, you may put the exiled card into its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nWhen Necrogen Scudder enters the battlefield, you lose 3 life.', 'Flying\\nWhen Resolute Archangel enters the battlefield, if your life total is less than your starting life total, it becomes equal to your starting life total.', 'Flying\\nWhen Siege Dragon enters the battlefield, destroy all Walls your opponents control.\\nWhenever Siege Dragon attacks, if defending player controls no Walls, it deals 2 damage to each creature without flying that player controls.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Kapsho Kitefins or another creature enters the battlefield under your control, tap target creature an opponent controls.', "Flying\\nWhenever Master of Predicaments deals combat damage to a player, choose a card in your hand. That player guesses whether the card's mana value is greater than 4. If the player guessed wrong, you may cast the card without paying its mana cost.", 'Flying\\n{5}{U}{U}: Draw a card for each color among permanents you control.\\n{5}{U}{U}, Exile Soul of Ravnica from your graveyard: Draw a card for each color among permanents you control.', 'Flying\\n{R}: Furnace Whelp gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'For each attacking creature, its owner puts it on the top or bottom of their library.', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', 'Heat Ray deals X damage to target creature.', "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\n{3}{B}: Until end of turn, Xathrid Slyblade loses hexproof and gains first strike and deathtouch. (It deals combat damage before creatures without first strike. Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)", 'If a source would deal damage to equipped creature, prevent X of that damage, where X is the number of creatures you control.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Indestructible\\n{T}: Add {C}.', "Intimidate (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)", "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\nAll lands are Islands in addition to their other types.\\nCreatures without flying or islandwalk can't attack.", 'Jorubai Murk Lurker gets +1/+1 as long as you control a Swamp.\\n{1}{B}: Target creature gains lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by the creature also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', "Juggernaut attacks each combat if able.\\nJuggernaut can't be blocked by Walls.", 'Kalonian Twingrove\'s power and toughness are each equal to the number of Forests you control.\\nWhen Kalonian Twingrove enters the battlefield, create a green Treefolk Warrior creature token with "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to the number of Forests you control."', "Kird Chieftain gets +1/+1 as long as you control a Forest.\\n{4}{G}: Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains trample until end of turn. (It can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", 'Lava Axe deals 5 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'Lifelink', 'Lightning Strike deals 3 damage to any target.', 'Nightfire Giant gets +1/+1 as long as you control a Mountain.\\n{4}{R}: Nightfire Giant deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Nonblack creatures get -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'Other Goblin creatures you control attack each combat if able.\\nAt the beginning of combat on your turn, create a 1/1 red Goblin creature token with haste.\\nWhenever Goblin Rabblemaster attacks, it gets +1/+0 until end of turn for each other attacking Goblin.', 'Other black creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{2}{B}, {T}: Another target black creature you control gains deathtouch until end of turn. (Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', 'Other blue creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{U}, {T}: Another target blue creature you control gains flying until end of turn.', "Other green creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{G}, {T}: Another target green creature you control gains trample until end of turn. (It can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", 'Other red creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{R}, {T}: Another target red creature you control gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', "Other white creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{W}, {T}: Another target white creature you control gains vigilance until end of turn. (Attacking doesn't cause it to tap.)", "Pay 2 life: Shadowcloak Vampire gains flying until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt by nongreen creatures this turn.', "Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control. Then that creature fights target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", "Put target creature into its owner's library second from the top.", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nWhenever Netcaster Spider blocks a creature with flying, Netcaster Spider gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Reach\\n{3}{G}{G}: Create a 3/3 green Beast creature token.\\n{3}{G}{G}, Exile Soul of Zendikar from your graveyard: Create a 3/3 green Beast creature token.', "Return target creature you control and target creature you don't control to their owners' hands.", "Return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand.", 'Return two target cards from your graveyard to your hand. Exile Restock.', "Return up to two target creatures to their owners' hands.", "Scuttling Doom Engine can't be blocked by creatures with power 2 or less.\\nWhen Scuttling Doom Engine dies, it deals 6 damage to target opponent or planeswalker.", 'Seismic Strike deals damage to target creature equal to the number of Mountains you control.', 'Sliver creatures you control have "When this creature enters the battlefield, you may exile target creature an opponent controls until this creature leaves the battlefield."', 'Sliver creatures you control have deathtouch. (Any amount of damage a creature with deathtouch deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', 'Sliver creatures you control have indestructible. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy them.)', "Sliver creatures you control have menace. (They can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", 'Sunblade Elf gets +1/+1 as long as you control a Plains.\\n{4}{W}: Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Target creature gains deathtouch until end of turn. Regenerate it. (The next time that creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat. Any amount of damage a creature with deathtouch deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)", 'Target creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -3/-3 until end of turn. You lose 3 life.', 'Target creature gets -5/-0 until end of turn.', "Target creature you control gets +1/+1 and gains hexproof until end of turn. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", 'Target opponent mills seven cards.', 'Target player discards two cards.', 'Target player draws two cards and loses 2 life.', 'Target player gains 2 life for each creature on the battlefield.', "This spell can't be countered.\\nTrample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nGlacial Crasher can't attack unless there is a Mountain on the battlefield.", 'Trample\\n{5}: Permanents you control gain indestructible until end of turn.\\n{5}, Exile Soul of New Phyrexia from your graveyard: Permanents you control gain indestructible until end of turn.', 'Undergrowth Scavenger enters the battlefield with a number of +1/+1 counters on it equal to the number of creature cards in all graveyards.', 'Until end of turn, each creature target player controls loses all abilities and becomes a blue Frog with base power and toughness 1/1.', 'Until end of turn, target creature loses all abilities and becomes a blue Frog with base power and toughness 1/1.', "Vigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)\\nWarden of the Beyond gets +2/+2 as long as an opponent owns a card in exile.", 'Vigilance\\n{4}{W}{W}: Creatures you control get +2/+2 and gain first strike and lifelink until end of turn.\\n{4}{W}{W}, Exile Soul of Theros from your graveyard: Creatures you control get +2/+2 and gain first strike and lifelink until end of turn.', 'When Black Cat dies, target opponent discards a card at random.', 'When Boonweaver Giant enters the battlefield, you may search your graveyard, hand, and/or library for an Aura card and put it onto the battlefield attached to Boonweaver Giant. If you search your library this way, shuffle.', 'When Forge Devil enters the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to target creature and 1 damage to you.', "When Frost Lynx enters the battlefield, tap target creature an opponent controls. That creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'When Gravedigger enters the battlefield, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', "When Heliod's Pilgrim enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an Aura card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.", "When Invasive Species enters the battlefield, return another permanent you control to its owner's hand.", 'When Kinsbaile Skirmisher enters the battlefield, target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'When Meteorite enters the battlefield, it deals 2 damage to any target.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', "When Necromancer's Assistant enters the battlefield, mill three cards.", "When Phytotitan dies, return it to the battlefield tapped under its owner's control at the beginning of their next upkeep.", 'When Radiant Fountain enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'When Reclamation Sage enters the battlefield, you may destroy target artifact or enchantment.', "When Rotfeaster Maggot enters the battlefield, exile target creature card from a graveyard. You gain life equal to that card's toughness.", 'When Satyr Wayfinder enters the battlefield, reveal the top four cards of your library. You may put a land card from among them into your hand. Put the rest into your graveyard.', 'When Shaman of Spring enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Tireless Missionaries enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.', 'When you cast this spell, reveal the top X cards of your library. You may put a nonland permanent card with mana value X or less from among them onto the battlefield. Then shuffle the rest into your library.\\nGenesis Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.', 'Whenever Borderland Marauder attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Whenever Frenzied Goblin attacks, you may pay {R}. If you do, target creature can't block this turn.", 'Whenever a Sliver creature you control becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter that spell or ability unless its controller pays {2}.', 'Whenever a Sliver you control attacks, defending player loses 1 life.', 'Whenever a creature an opponent controls dies, Altac Bloodseeker gets +2/+0 and gains first strike and haste until end of turn. (It deals combat damage before creatures without first strike, and it can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', "Whenever a creature card is put into an opponent's graveyard from anywhere, you gain 1 life.", 'Whenever a creature without flying attacks you or a planeswalker you control, Circle of Flame deals 1 damage to that creature.', 'Whenever a nontoken creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {W}. If you do, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.\\n{1}{W}, Sacrifice a Spirit: Target non-Spirit creature gains indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it.)', 'Whenever an Aura becomes attached to Brood Keeper, create a 2/2 red Dragon creature token with flying. It has "{R}: This creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn."', 'Whenever an opponent discards a creature card, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\nWhenever an opponent discards a land card, add {B}{B}.\\nWhenever an opponent discards a noncreature, nonland card, draw a card.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, untap Midnight Guard.', 'Whenever another creature with power 3 or greater enters the battlefield under your control, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever another red creature enters the battlefield under your control, Foundry Street Denizen gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "Whenever you activate an ability of an artifact, if it isn't a mana ability, you may pay {R}. If you do, copy that ability. You may choose new targets for the copy.", 'Whenever you attack with two or more creatures, draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast a black spell or a Swamp enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever you cast a blue spell or an Island enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever you cast a green spell or a Forest enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever you cast a red spell or a Mountain enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever you cast a white spell or a Plains enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.', "Whenever you draw a card, put a +1/+1 counter on Chasm Skulker.\\nWhen Chasm Skulker dies, create X 1/1 blue Squid creature tokens with islandwalk, where X is the number of +1/+1 counters on Chasm Skulker. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", "Whenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on Ajani's Pridemate.", "You can't play lands.\\nSacrifice a land: Draw two cards. Activate only once each turn.", 'You may have Mercurial Pretender enter the battlefield as a copy of a creature you control, except it has "{2}{U}{U}: Return this creature to its owner\'s hand."', "[+1]: Chandra, Pyromaster deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker and 1 damage to up to one target creature that player or that planeswalker's controller controls. That creature can't block this turn.\\n[0]: Exile the top card of your library. You may play it this turn.\\n[−7]: Exile the top ten cards of your library. Choose an instant or sorcery card exiled this way and copy it three times. You may cast the copies without paying their mana costs.", '[+1]: Destroy another target planeswalker.\\n[+1]: Create a 3/3 black Beast creature token with deathtouch.\\n[−3]: Destroy target creature. You gain life equal to its toughness.\\n[−8]: Target opponent gets an emblem with "Whenever a creature attacks you, it gets +5/+5 and gains trample until end of turn."', "[+1]: Look at the top two cards of your library. Put one of them into your graveyard.\\n[−3]: Return another target nonland permanent to its owner's hand.\\n[−8]: Each player shuffles their hand and graveyard into their library. You draw seven cards.", "[+1]: Target land you control becomes a 4/4 Elemental creature with trample. It's still a land.\\n[+1]: Untap up to four target Forests.\\n[−7]: Search your library for any number of basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle. Those lands become 4/4 Elemental creatures with trample. They're still lands.", '[+1]: Target player discards a card.\\n[−2]: Search your library for a card, then shuffle and put that card on top.\\n[−8]: Put all creature cards from all graveyards onto the battlefield under your control.', '[+1]: Until end of turn, up to one target creature gets +1/+1 and gains first strike, vigilance, and lifelink.\\n[−2]: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control and a loyalty counter on each other planeswalker you control.\\n[−7]: You get an emblem with "If a source would deal damage to you or a planeswalker you control, prevent all but 1 of that damage."', '{1}{B}, Discard a creature card: Draw a card. If the discarded card was a Zombie card, create a tapped 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', '{1}{B}, Sacrifice another creature: Put a +1/+1 counter on Blood Host and you gain 2 life.', '{1}{W}, Sacrifice Selfless Cathar: Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{2}: Target creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{2}{B}: Zof Shade gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{2}{G}, {T}, Put a verse counter on Yisan, the Wanderer Bard: Search your library for a creature card with mana value equal to the number of verse counters on Yisan, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', "{2}{R}: Miner's Bane gets +1/+0 and gains trample until end of turn. (It can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", '{2}{U}, {T}, Sacrifice another creature: Reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a nonlegendary creature card. Put that card onto the battlefield and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', "{2}{U}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", '{3}{U}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{4}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{5}, {T}, Exile Perilous Vault: Exile all nonland permanents.', '{5}{G}{G}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Carnivorous Moss-Beast.', '{B}, {T}, Pay 1 life: Put a +1/+1 counter on Cruel Sadist.\\n{2}{B}, {T}, Remove X +1/+1 counters from Cruel Sadist: It deals X damage to target creature.', "{G}: Regenerate Ancient Silverback. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", '{R}, Sacrifice Torch Fiend: Destroy target artifact.', '{T}, Discard a card: Draw a card.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice Generator Servant: Add {C}{C}. If that mana is spent on a creature spell, it gains haste until end of turn. (That creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', "{T}, Sacrifice Tormod's Crypt: Exile target player's graveyard.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast a Sliver spell.\\n{5}, {T}: Create a 1/1 colorless Sliver creature token. Activate only if you control a Sliver.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}. Llanowar Wastes deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}. Yavimaya Coast deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}. Battlefield Forge deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}. Shivan Reef deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}. Caves of Koilos deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Put a charge counter on Grindclock.\\n{T}: Target player mills X cards, where X is the number of charge counters on Grindclock.', '{T}: You gain 1 life.']
flavor: ['"All peoples treasure a place where the weary traveler may drink in peace."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"All tinkerers have their heads in the clouds. I don\'t intend to stop there."', '"An angel\'s skull is left too plain by death. I made a few aesthetic modifications."\\n—Dommique, blood artist', '"And if I\'m lying," he began . . .', '"As our numbers dwindle, the ranks of the dead grow ever stronger."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"Boom! Boom! Boots the size of oxcarts, then an axe like a falling sun. Elves scattered. Trees scattered. Even the hills ran for the hills!"\\n—*Clachan Tales*', '"Brute force can sometimes kick down a locked door, but knowledge is a skeleton key."', '"Come, little one. Unfurl your wings, fill your lungs, and release your first fiery breath."', '"Comin\' through!" Designed by James Ernest', '"Don\'t worry, there\'s plenty for everyone."\\n—Vickon, Eleventh Company battlemage', '"Encase yourself in the most elaborate armor, and cower behind the heaviest shield. I would hate for you to feel helpless."\\n—Korig the Ruiner', '"Even your shadow is too foul to tolerate."', '"Feeding a normal army is a problem of logistics. With zombies, it is an asset. Feeding is why they fight. Feeding is why they are feared."\\n—Jadar, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"Guilty."', '"He has learned much in his long years. And unlike selfish humans, he\'s willing to share."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"Healing is more art than magic. Well, there is still quite a bit of magic."', '"I have seen countless petty warmongers gaze on it for a time before turning away."\\n—Sarlena, paladin of the Northern Verge', '"I\'m raising an army. Any volunteers?"', '"I\'ve never been above throwing the first punch."', '"I\'ve tried so many variations on how to get rid of annoying things that it\'s hard to decide which one I like best."\\n—Ashurel, voidmage', '"If I fail to offer myself, we will surely be overrun. My fate would be the same."', '"If a boggart even dares breathe near one of my kin, I\'ll know. And I\'ll not be happy."', '"If it were merely lethal, that would be sufficient. The art, however, is in maximizing the suffering it causes."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"If you cannot turn your enemy\'s strength to weakness, then make that strength your own."\\n—Gresha, warrior sage', '"Impossible! How could they overwhelm us? We had barricades, war elephants, . . . and they were barely a tenth of our number!"\\n—General Avitora', '"In a daze, I woke and looked upon the battlefield, where I could swear my dreams were laying waste to the enemy."\\n—Letter from a soldier', '"In the gathering there is strength for all who founder, renewal for all who languish, love for all who sing."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 642', '"It saddens me to lose a source of inspiration. This one seemed especially promising."\\n—Ashiok', '"It\'s a truly disconcerting sight to see their shadows cast upon the deck."\\n—Captain Triff', '"Let nothing own the skies but the wind."\\n—Dejara, Giltwood druid', '"Life grows everywhere. My kin merely find those places where it grows strongest."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"Life up here is simple. Adapt to the ways of the mountains and they will reward you. Fight them and they will end you."\\n—Kezim, prodigal pyromancer', '"My favorite guilty pleasure? Are there innocent ones?"', '"Pain is temporary. So is life."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Pyrotechnic activity of any sort is strictly prohibited. It is irrelevant that today is a holiday."', '"Ribbit."', '"Seeing one slowly devour one of my party begged the question—do they know what cruelty is?"\\n—Hastric, Thunian scout', '"Soulless demon, you are bound to me. Now we will both dwell in oblivion."', '"Still alive? No matter. I\'ll leave you as a warning to others who would oppose me."\\n—Vish Kal, Blood Arbiter', '"The battle is won. There\'s work to be done. / The Blessed Sleep must wait. / A fiend is about. It stalks the devout. / I\'ll save them from my fate."\\n—"The Good Geist\'s Vow"', '"The cathars have their swords, the inquisitors their axes. I prefer the \'diplomatic\' approach."\\n—Terhold, archmage of Drunau', '"The centaurs are truly free. Never will they be tamed by temptation or controlled by fear. They live in total harmony, a feat not yet achieved by our kind."\\n—Ramal, sage of Westgate', '"The dragon is a perfect marriage of power and the will to use it."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"The flies were bothering me."\\n—Jalira, master polymorphist', '"The hive shimmered, and its walls seemed a living mirror."\\n—Hastric, Thunian scout', '"The key to unlocking this puzzle is within you."\\n—Doriel, mentor of Mistral Isle', '"The law has its place—as a footnote in my spellbook."\\n—Siyani, fugitive mage', '"The sea blesses the tiny with the power to fell the mighty."\\n—Talrand, sky summoner', '"The slivers became adept at provoking a fear response in other species."\\n—Hastric, Thunian scout', '"The vaulted ceiling of our faith rests upon such pillars."\\n—Darugand, banisher priest', '"There are those who do not believe in the existence of the amphin. This seems somehow to be of their own design."\\n—Gor Muldrak, *Cryptohistories*', '"There was clearly a scream. I\'m not sure if there was a mouth."\\n—Sachir, Akoum Expeditionary House', '"There\'s never a good time for a disaster or an attack. That\'s why we\'re here."\\n—Oren, militia captain', '"They\'re easy enough to find. Question is, are you sure you want to find one?"\\n—Juruk, Kalonian tracker', '"Thieves and squid squirm the same way when you capture them."', '"Thirsty?"\\n—Drunvalus, hydromancer', '"This abomination never belonged in our world. I\'m merely setting it free."\\n—Dierk, geistmage', '"This is the source, the line unbroken since the calamity that brought such monsters to our shores."\\n—Hastric, Thunian scout', '"Though tempered differently, all wills can be broken."\\n—Inquisitor Kyrik', '"To be in the presence of a revoker is to be truly alone."\\n—Kara Vrist, Neurok agent', '"We attacked with arrows dipped in poison. The slivers that did not die began to change."\\n—Hastric, Thunian scout', '"We patrol the steppes to keep enemies from the forest verge."', '"What was once formed by masons, shaped by smiths, or given life by mages, I will return to the embrace of the earth."', '"What you are attempting is not against the law. It is, however, extremely foolish."', '"When one of us prospers, the pride prospers."\\n—Jazal Goldmane', '"When you\'re on watch, no noise is harmless and no shadow can be ignored."\\n—Olgard of the Skiltfolk', '"When your cities and trinkets crumble, only nature will remain."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"Which do you think is a better deterrent: a moat of water or one of fire?"\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"Why do guards always look surprised when we bash them?" asked Ruric. "I think they expect a bribe," said Thar.', '"With rage as your forge, your hammer can smite anything."', '"Yawgmoth\'s corpse is a wound in the universe. His foul blood seeps out, infecting the land with his final curse."\\n—Lord Windgrace', '"You can become anything if I just put my mind to it."', '"You don\'t survive in the wild by standing in plain sight."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"You don\'t want to know what happens after I put on the goggles."', '"You will be reimbursed for your donation."\\n"The reimbursement is spiritual."\\n—Temple signs', '"Your mind was a curious mix of madness and genius. I just took away the genius."\\n—Jace Beleren', 'A bit of pain never hurts.', "A forest fire can rejuvenate the land, but the tar's vile consumption leaves the land forever ruined.", 'A grave is not always for burial.', 'A masterwork of spite, inspired by madness.', 'A strict upgrade over the cinder hatchet.', 'A symbol of ambition in ruthless times.', 'A symbol of conviction in uncertain times.', 'A symbol of ferocity in oppressive times.', 'A symbol of passion in indifferent times.', 'A symbol of sagacity in bewildering times.', 'After the Battle of Pharagax Bridge, the Champion spent many months among the leonin of Oreskos. She found that they were quick to take offense, not because they were thin-skinned, but because they were always eager for a fight.\\n—*The Theriad*', 'After the Foundry Street riot, Arrester Hulbein tried to ban bludgeons. Which, inevitably, resulted in another riot.', 'An eye for detail, a mind for numbers, a soul of clockwork.', 'An oath of fealty sworn with a handshake.', 'An overwhelming sense of calm accompanies the gryffs that wheel above the roofs of Gavony.', 'Arrive for worship. Leave for war.', 'Astride the bucking creature, Gribble hurtled down the mountainside while his Grotag brethren cheered. It was at that moment that the legend of the Skrill Tamer was born.', 'At the instant of death, the mystery of life.', "Baby dragons can't figure out humans—if they didn't want to be killed, why were they made of meat and treasure?", 'Beyond pain, beyond obsession and wild despair, there lies a place of twisted power only the most tormented souls can reach.', "Contrary to popular belief, it's kept aloft by necrogen gas, not the screaming agony of a thousand murdered souls.", 'Cut it down, bury it in snow, put it to the torch. The rose will still bloom again.', 'Designed by Brad Muir', 'Designed by Brian Fargo', 'Designed by David Sirlin', 'Designed by George Fan', 'Designed by Justin Gary', 'Designed by Markus Persson', 'Designed by Mike Neumann', 'Designed by Penny Arcade', 'Designed by Rob Pardo', 'Designed by Stone Librande', 'Designed by the Magic community', 'Devils redecorate every room with fire.', "Dominaria's most extravagant crypt nevertheless holds an empty grave.", 'Empires rise and fall, but evil is eternal.', 'Face of innocence. Hand of death. Designed by Edmund McMillen', 'Find your center, and you will find your way.', "First you lose your enemy's trail. Then you lose all sense of direction. Then you hear the growls . . .", 'Follow the light. In its absence, follow her.', 'Fortified by the wilds.', 'He draws strength from a vast source few mortals can fathom. Designed by Isaiah Cartwright', 'He just likes to break legs. Collecting the debt is a bonus.', 'He who hesitates is lunch.', 'If they succeed in their holy work, their order will vanish into welcome obscurity, for there will be no more souls to redeem.', 'Is it at the top of the food chain or the bottom?', 'It is an expert at culling individuals who stray too far from the herd.', 'It readily attacks much larger prey, knowing retaliation is impossible.', 'It requires immense pressure to imbue an item with magic. If the spell is broken . . .', 'It sees a rotting carcass as a good wine which has been aged properly.', 'It would be ill-mannered to decline his invitation. It would be ill-advised to accept it.', "It's easier to relocate a village that lies in their path than to turn the bugs aside.", 'Its footfalls cause violent earthquakes, hurtling boulders, and unseasonable dust storms.', 'Its last life is spent tormenting your dreams.', 'Its root system spans the entire floor of the jungle, making eradication impossible.', 'Kidnappers caught in Havengul are given two choices: languish in prison or become rat catchers. The smart ones go to prison.', 'Like a meteor, it strikes from above without warning. Unlike a meteor, it then carries you off and eats you.', 'Like blinking or breathing, responding to an alarm is an involuntary reflex.', 'Little agonies pave the way to greater power.', 'Many a besieged city has surrendered upon hearing the distinctive rumble of the juggernaut.', 'Many have heard the slither of dragging armor and the soft squelch of its voice. But only its victims ever meet its icy gaze.', 'Masters of the arcane savor a delicious irony. Their study of deep and complex arcana leads to such a simple end: the ability to say merely yes or no.', 'Mercy is for those who keep their distance.', 'Mulch is the fabric of life in the forest. Plants live in it, they die in it, and then they become part of it, feeding countless generations to come.', 'Nature is itself wild—in all its forms.', 'Nightfire turns the greatest weakness of the undead into formidable strength.', 'Of royal blood among the spirits of the air, the Mahamoti djinn rides on the wings of the winds. As dangerous in the gambling hall as he is in battle, he is a master of trickery and misdirection.', 'Once a year, the skies over Paliano fill with the flying machines of those who hope to be taken on as pupils by the artificer Muzzio.', 'Pray you never hear it chime.', 'Professional pilferers prefer proper preparation.', 'Ranger wisdom dictates that when fleeing from a moss-beast, you must stay calm, find your bearings, and run south.', 'Sailors have come to regard them as bad luck, for they falsely bring hope of land.', 'Shades are drawn to places of power, often rooting themselves in a single area to feed.', 'Sins that would be too gruesome in the light of day are made more pleasing in the dark of night.', 'Slivers are often seen toying with enemies they capture, not out of cruelty, but to fully learn their physical capabilities.', "Some bog witches practice the strange art of batrachomancy, reading portents in the number, size, and color of warts on a toad's hide.", "Some shamanic sects advocate the different seasons, each working to preserve nature's cycles.", 'Stand your post for duty. Stand your ground for honor.', 'Structures built from darksteel yield to neither assault nor age.', 'The Champion stood alone between the horde of the Returned and the shrine to Karametra, cutting down scores among hundreds. She would have been overcome if not for the aid of the temple guardians whom Karametra awakened.\\n—*The Theriad*', 'The Conclave acts with a single will, expressed by countless warriors.', 'The Onakke were masters of dark arts and artifice. Their creations continue to spread foul magic, paving the way for their return.', "The beating of a gargoyle's wings on the air is like the cracking of stones. Intruders who rouse a gargoyle are certain to hear the cracking of bones.", 'The blessings of Heliod are apparent for all to see.', 'The dead serve as their own tombstones.', 'The death of a scout can be as informative as a safe return.', 'The experiments decided to perform some research of their own.', 'The first satyr to wake after a revel must search for the site of the next one.', 'The giant was felt a few seconds before he was seen.', 'The king went off to find himself. Imagine his terror when he succeeded.', 'The knights of Troinir Keep took the rhino as their emblem due to its intense focus when charging down a perceived threat—a trait they discovered on a hunting excursion.', 'The magic of the elves leaves its mark on the forest. The magic of the forest leaves its mark on the animals who live there. The animals of the forest leave their mark on all who trespass.', 'The massive dominate through might. The tiny survive with guile. Beware the tiny who become massive.', "The modular nature of the automaton's design makes assembly perfectly intuitive.", 'The people of the Sevick Isles have a unique understanding of the term "ominous clouds."', 'The promise of anguish is payment enough for services rendered.', 'The sacred feathers of the pegasus are said to have healing powers.', 'The spirit dragon Ugin arranged the hedrons of Zendikar to direct leylines of energy. To disrupt one is to unleash devastation and chaos.', 'The thunder of its hooves beats dreams into despair.', 'The undisputed master of the mountains of Shiv.', 'There are certain stones even dwarves know to leave in the earth.', 'There are many words and phrases that can cause an experienced wizard to tremble in fear. Chief among them is "oops."', 'There will always be those who presume to improve nature, or dare to befoul it. And nature will always have a response.', 'Though she is rightly feared, there are relatively few tales of her deeds in battle, for few survive her raids.', 'Timing is everything.', "To a goblin, value is based on the four S's: shiny, stabby, smelly, and super smelly.", 'To know the battlefield is to anticipate the enemy. To know the enemy is to anticipate victory.', 'To wield lightning is to tame chaos.', 'Too often, some self-described genius comes up with a "labor-saving device" that ends up creating far more work.', 'Trespassers are welcome to try.', "Verick held his breath. Breathing wouldn't reveal his position, but it would force him to smell the goblins.", 'We are made stronger by those we fight for. Designed by Richard Garriott', 'What he lacks in stature, he makes up for with enthusiasm.', 'What looked like a retreat was actually a replenishing.', 'When carrion feeds on carrion, dark days approach.', 'With an armory of light, even the squire may champion her people.', 'Without the interfering hands of civilization, nature will always shape itself to its own needs.', 'You need only raise your spear to receive this blessing.', 'Zombies and necromancers agree: easy access to brains is preferred.']
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Adam Paquette', 'Adam Rex', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Allen Williams', 'Andreas Rocha', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Ash Wood', 'Austin Hsu', 'Ben Thompson', 'Brad Rigney', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Brian Despain', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chase Stone', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'Daarken', 'Dan Dos Santos', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'Dermot Power', 'Dominick Domingo', 'Donato Giancola', 'Drew Baker', 'Erica Yang', 'Eytan Zana', 'Filip Burburan', 'Florian de Gesincourt', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Goran Josic', 'Greg Staples', 'Hideaki Takamura', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Ryman', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Rainville', 'Jasper Sandner', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Nelson', 'Johann Bodin', 'Johannes Voss', 'John Avon', 'John Severin Brassell', 'John Stanko', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Julie Dillon', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Marco Nelor', 'Mark Winters', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael C. Hayes', 'Michael Komarck', 'Mike Bierek', 'Min Yum', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Pete Venters', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Phill Simmer', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ryan Alexander Lee', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sam Burley', 'Sam Wood', 'Scott Chou', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Scott Murphy', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Stephan Martiniere', 'Steve Luke', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Thomas Denmark', 'Tim Hildebrandt', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Vance Kovacs', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Wesley Burt', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yohann Schepacz', 'Zack Stella', 'Zoltan Boros', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai']
